Suppose that the least common multiple of the first $25$ positive integers is equal to $26A7114B4C0$. Find $100 \\times A + 10 \\times B + C$.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"e7465922015f399a7547e7c1d07849b854c39af7af6272375cf9401c54a455e0"},"seconds":50.118595123291016,"seed":846660893807486716,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we first need to understand the least common multiple (LCM) of the first 25 positive integers. The LCM of a set of integers is the smallest positive integer that is divisible by each of the integers in the set.\n\nThe prime factorization of the LCM of the first 25 positive integers is determined by the highest powers of all primes less than or equal to 25. The primes less than or equal to 25 are 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, and 23. The highest powers of these primes within the range of the first 25 positive integers are as follows:\n- The highest power of 2 is $2^4 = 16$ (since $2^5 = 32 > 25$).\n- The highest power of 3 is $3^2 = 9$ (since $3^3 = 27 > 25$).\n- The highest power of 5 is $5^2 = 25$ (since $5^3 = 125 > 25$).\n- The highest power of 7 is $7^1 = 7$.\n- The highest power of 11 is $11^1 = 11$.\n- The highest power of 13 is $13^1 = 13$.\n- The highest power of 17 is $17^1 = 17$.\n- The highest power of 19 is $19^1 = 19$.\n- The highest power of 23 is $23^1 = 23$.\n\nThus, the LCM of the first 25 positive integers is:\n\\[ 2^4 \\times 3^2 \\times 5^2 \\times 7 \\times 11 \\times 13 \\times 17 \\times 19 \\times 23 \\]\n\nCalculating this product step-by-step:\n\\[ 2^4 = 16 \\]\n\\[ 3^2 = 9 \\]\n\\[ 5^2 = 25 \\]\n\\[ 16 \\times 9 = 144 \\]\n\\[ 144 \\times 25 = 3600 \\]\n\\[ 3600 \\times 7 = 25200 \\]\n\\[ 25200 \\times 11 = 277200 \\]\n\\[ 277200 \\times 13 = 3603600 \\]\n\\[ 3603600 \\times 17 = 61261200 \\]\n\\[ 61261200 \\times 19 = 1163962800 \\]\n\\[ 1163962800 \\times 23 = 26771144400 \\]\n\nSo, the LCM of the first 25 positive integers is 26771144400, which matches the given form 26A7114B4C0. By comparing, we can see that A = 7, B = 4, and C = 0.\n\nThus, the value of $100 \\times A + 10 \\times B + C$ is:\n\\[ 100 \\times 7 + 10 \\times 4 + 0 = 700 + 40 + 0 = 740 \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{740}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{740}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
